WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.008
How an annuity works.

2
00:00:02.555 --> 00:00:05.259
Life insurance protects against dying too soon.

3
00:00:05.713 --> 00:00:10.813
An annuity protects against the opposite risk: living too long and running out of

4
00:00:10.833 --> 00:00:12.028
money.

5
00:00:12.966 --> 00:00:15.113
Every annuity has two phases.

6
00:00:15.288 --> 00:00:17.539
The first is the accumulation period.

7
00:00:17.714 --> 00:00:19.455
The owner pays in premiums,

8
00:00:19.584 --> 00:00:23.391
either as a single lump sum or as flexible payments over time,

9
00:00:23.519 --> 00:00:25.898
and the earnings grow tax-deferred.

10
00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:29.869
An immediate annuity skips ahead: it's bought with one premium,

11
00:00:29.893 --> 00:00:32.168
and income begins within one year.

12
00:00:32.401 --> 00:00:34.617
A deferred annuity starts paying later.

13
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:40.190
And withdrawing money early from a deferred annuity can trigger surrender charges.

14
00:00:41.131 --> 00:00:45.403
The second phase is the annuity period, also called the payout period.

15
00:00:45.949 --> 00:00:49.470
When the owner annuitizes, which is usually irrevocable,

16
00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:53.680
the accumulated value is converted into a stream of regular income payments,

17
00:00:53.704 --> 00:00:56.420
and those payments can be guaranteed for life.

18
00:00:57.399 --> 00:01:01.090
Payout options rank the same way as life insurance settlement options.

19
00:01:01.753 --> 00:01:04.898
Life only pays the most each month, but stops at death.

20
00:01:05.352 --> 00:01:08.984
Life with period certain guarantees payments for a set number of years.

21
00:01:09.531 --> 00:01:14.128
A refund life annuity guarantees that at least the premium paid comes back.

22
00:01:14.489 --> 00:01:19.178
And joint and survivor, which pays until the last of two annuitants dies,

23
00:01:19.539 --> 00:01:20.525
pays the least.

24
00:01:21.071 --> 00:01:24.019
More guarantees mean smaller payments.

25
00:01:24.963 --> 00:01:28.097
In Arizona, an annuity's free look is ten days,

26
00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:31.092
or thirty days if the owner is sixty-five or older.

27
00:01:31.546 --> 00:01:35.648
And if the buyer's guide and disclosure document weren't provided at or before the

28
00:01:35.668 --> 00:01:38.778
application, the free look is at least fifteen days.

29
00:01:39.139 --> 00:01:42.842
Remember: life insurance protects against dying too soon.

30
00:01:43.017 --> 00:01:45.733
Annuities protect against living too long.
